From: Aurélien Pommel <aurelien.pommel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip: inno-usb2: power the OTG port on before charger detection

Booted with no cable, the port is suspended (phy_sus 0x1d1), and charger
detection run in that state times out and reports a DCP: a computer plugged
in later never gets SDP, so the gadget is never bound. With the cable in at
boot, the port is powered and SDP is found.

---
--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
@@ -705,6 +705,7 @@
 			dev_dbg(&rport->phy->dev, "vbus_attach\n");
 			switch (rphy->chg_state) {
 			case USB_CHG_STATE_UNDEFINED:
+				rockchip_usb2phy_power_on(rport->phy);
 				schedule_delayed_work(&rport->chg_work, 0);
 				return;
 			case USB_CHG_STATE_DETECTED:
